narrative:
## Building a Digital Fortune Teller

Now you know both random numbers AND if/elif statements. It's time to combine them into something fun! Your fortune teller will randomly pick from a list of fortunes and display one.

### How It Works

```xiom
fn main() {
  let roll: Int = math.random_range(1, 3);
  io.println("Your fortune cookie says...");

  if roll == 1 {
    io.println("An exciting adventure is coming your way!");
  } elif roll == 2 {
    io.println("A surprise gift will arrive soon.");
  } else {
    io.println("Today is your lucky day — take a chance!");
  }
}
```

The program generates a random number 1 to 3, then uses `if/elif/else` to pick the matching fortune. The `elif` (else-if) checks a second condition if the first one is false. The `else` at the end catches anything that didn't match — in this case, when `roll` is 3.

Run it a few times. You'll get different fortunes each time. You've just built your own fortune cookie!

